# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Subgeneratorr's images run on Linux, so shell scripts and entrypoints
# must use LF. On Windows, git's autocrlf can rewrite them to CRLF on
# checkout, which breaks shebang resolution inside the Linux image: the
# kernel looks for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r" and the
# container dies in a restart loop with:
#
#     exec /entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# See https://github.com/tylerbcrawford/subgeneratorr/issues/1
#
# Default: auto-detect text vs binary, and check out every text file with
# LF on all platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that MUST be LF to execute or build correctly in a Linux container.
*.sh         text eol=lf
Dockerfile   text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary assets git must never line-ending-convert.
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
